@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Bill Occurrence Correction — Manual Validation Matrix
+
+Use this only after the user deploys the reviewed source to the bounded project.
+Do not run automated writers against the bounded workbook. Choose real entries
+whose expected values are known, record before-values first, and finish each
+journey before starting the next.
+
+**Important distinction:** changing a payment amount keeps that occurrence
+handled and hidden from Bills. The occurrence returns to Bills only when the
+user explicitly chooses **Remove payment**, which reverses the selected
+payment contribution while retaining immutable Activity history.
+
+## Required visual journeys
+
+| Case | User steps | Expected Bills result | Expected Activity result | Expected financial result |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| M1 — Manual Pay, cash | In Bills, choose a dated cash-funded occurrence, select **Pay**, confirm amount/date, and save | The exact occurrence clears; future occurrences remain | One customer-facing payment row has **Correct entry**; no separate paid-marker row is shown | The correct Cash Flow month increases by the entered expense amount |
+| M2 — Change Manual Pay amount | From M1 Activity, choose **Correct entry**, **Change amount**, enter a different positive amount, choose a reason, and submit | The occurrence stays handled and does **not** return to Bills | Original action is superseded; one corrected replacement is actionable; success shows the corrected amount and current Cash Flow value | Only the original payment contribution changes; unrelated values remain |
+| M3 — Remove Manual Pay | Correct the M2 replacement, choose **Remove payment**, add a reason, and submit | The exact occurrence returns to Bills as a manual-attention card without a page reload | The replacement shows **Payment removed**; immutable correction history remains | The recorded Bill payment contribution is removed and the exact prior cell state is restored |
+| M4 — Re-pay after removal | Pay the restored M3 occurrence once | The occurrence clears once and does not duplicate | A new payment operation appears; the removed history remains read-only | Cash Flow receives exactly one new payment contribution |
+| M5 — Duplicate/retry guard | Double-click is prevented by the busy state; after completion, try an old/stale Pay action only if one is still visible | No duplicate card transition or payment | No duplicate operation is added | Cash Flow and any linked balance change once |
+| S1 — Skip | On a different dated occurrence choose **Skip** and confirm | Only that occurrence clears; future occurrences remain | One Skip row offers **Correct entry** | No payment is recorded; a blank target may display `$0.00` under existing Skip behavior |
+| S2 — Remove Skip | Correct S1 and choose **Remove skip** | The exact occurrence returns | Skip shows **Skip removed**; Change amount is not offered | No payment or debt change occurs |
+| A1 — AutoPay amount change | Use an eligible fixed AutoPay bill whose due occurrence has been applied, then correct its Activity row to a different amount | Occurrence remains handled | Original is superseded by one actionable AutoPay replacement | Cash Flow reflects the corrected AutoPay amount |
+| A2 — Remove AutoPay | Correct the A1 replacement and choose **Remove payment** | The occurrence returns immediately and is not automatically applied again | Replacement shows **Payment removed** | AutoPay contribution is removed and stays removed |
+| C1 — Credit-card-linked Manual Pay | Pay a dated Bill whose payee matches a tracked credit-card debt, then change its amount | Occurrence clears | Correction preview/result shows both Cash Flow and linked card/debt impacts | Cash Flow and debt balance change together by the corrected delta |
+| C2 — Remove credit-card payment | Remove the C1 replacement | Occurrence returns | Row shows **Payment removed** with immutable history | Both Cash Flow and linked debt balance return to their verified pre-payment values |
+| L1 — Later-entry preservation | Pay a Bill, then add another Quick Add to the same payee/month; correct or remove only the earlier Bill payment | Bill occurrence follows only the selected correction | Later Quick Add remains independently actionable | The later Quick Add amount remains in Cash Flow |
+| F1 — Changed-state refusal | After a test payment, deliberately change its linked Cash Flow cell outside CashCompass, then open **Correct entry** | No occurrence transition | Preview refuses safely and asks for review/refresh | CashCompass does not overwrite the externally changed value |
+
+## Visual quality checks
+
+- The drawer eyebrow says **BILL OCCURRENCE**.
+- Manual Pay and AutoPay offer **Change amount** and **Remove payment**.
+- Skip offers **Remove skip** only.
+- Remove help explains that the occurrence returns without automatic payment.
+- Success uses **Amount changed**, **Payment removed**, or **Skip removed**.
+- Activity shows one customer-facing Manual Pay row, not a second internal
+  `bill_paid` marker row.
+- Corrected originals are not actionable; their current replacement is.
+- Dates use the intended local calendar day and amounts are positive in the
+  correction form.
+- No raw worksheet name, stack trace, stuck spinner, yellow false-conflict
+  warning, horizontal overflow, or duplicate success message appears.
+
+## Bounded impact to validate
+
+This feature changes Bill write coordination and occurrence-state rules. It
+does not change workbook columns, formulas, formatting definitions,
+administrator identity, or stored Bill recurrence configuration. The user
+should validate only the selected occurrence, its Cash Flow month, an optional
+linked credit-card balance, and the corresponding Activity history.
