+### REG-041 — Bill money and occurrence state could complete separately
+- Category: REGRESSION / FINANCIAL SAFETY / COMPOUND BILL OPERATION
+- Date discovered: 2026-07-29
+- Status: fixed locally; isolated Central runtime confirmation pending
+- Affected files: `dashboard_data.js`, `quick_add_payment.js`,
+  `activity_log.js`, Bills/Activity dashboard scripts, Bills Pay Harness, and
+  Populated Dashboard E2E
+- Root cause: Manual Pay recorded Cash Flow and its handled-occurrence marker in
+  separate server requests, while Skip and AutoPay lacked one exact
+  before/after operation envelope. A partial failure could therefore leave
+  money and occurrence state out of agreement, and Activity could not safely
+  change or reopen the complete occurrence.
+- Expected result: dated Manual Pay uses one lock, one server-generated
+  operation ID, exact financial targets, and one occurrence target. Skip and
+  AutoPay record the same exact-state contract. Any failed compound operation
+  compensates its in-flight financial writes and Activity rows. Activity can
+  change Manual Pay/AutoPay amounts or reopen them; Skip is reopen-only.
+  Reopened occurrences return to Bills and suppress automatic reapplication.
+- Permanent coverage: the registered Bills Pay E2E uses only its
+  marker-verified disposable workbook to prove shared Manual Pay evidence,
+  duplicate refusal, later-entry preservation, amount change, replacement
+  correction, Manual Pay/Skip/AutoPay reopen, card return, and AutoPay append
+  compensation. Populated Dashboard E2E changes and reopens Manual Pay through
+  the real Activity drawer, then verifies Cash Flow and Bills card state.
+
+### REG-042 — Browser-driven Bill correction validation could run for hours without a valid reopen
+- Category: REGRESSION / TEST HARNESS / VALIDATION RELIABILITY
+- Date discovered: 2026-07-29
+- Status: fixed; isolated Central `@253` server and visual runtime PASS
+- Affected files: Bills Pay Harness scenario/suite, Populated Dashboard E2E
+  server adapter/control page/browser assertion, Validation console evidence,
+  and permanent Harness/P1 regression checks
+- Root cause: the focused browser journey performed the complete compound
+  financial workflow through multiple Apps Script callbacks and polling loops.
+  Its reopen steps also supplied custom strings such as `Payment reversed` as
+  the reason enum even though production accepts only the four drawer options.
+  The invalid dropdown value became blank, so the server correctly refused every
+  reopen while the browser kept waiting for a receipt that could never arrive.
+- Expected result: the registered server scenario is authoritative for all
+  financial mutations and uses `Other` plus a custom note when needed. It has a
+  stable 21-assertion budget, phase deadlines, single-flight execution, durable
+  privacy-safe receipts, and verified cleanup. The browser performs one
+  server-prepared Manual Pay and read-only drawer inspection only.
+- Permanent coverage: static Harness/P1 checks reject unsupported custom reason
+  values, browser correction submission, missing deadline/single-flight/durable
+  evidence contracts, and caller-selected workbook/financial inputs. Isolated
+  `@253` passed two consecutive server runs (21/21 in 81.527 s and 56.269 s)
+  plus focused visual run
+  `FR-af4bea15-1006-4922-8da3-2e516b35a544` in 52.329 s; every fixture was
+  Restricted and verified in Trash.
+
+### REG-043 — Bill payment removal did not preserve the complete repay journey
+- Category: REGRESSION / FINANCIAL SAFETY / UI RELIABILITY / TEST COVERAGE
+- Date discovered: 2026-07-29
+- Status: fixed; isolated Central `@259` server and browser runtime PASS
+- Affected files: Bill correction coordinator and Activity presentation,
+  Cash Flow operation state, Bills Due marker identity, same-page dashboard
+  refresh, Bills Pay server scenario, focused browser journey, and permanent
+  dashboard/Harness/P1 regression checks
+- Root cause: the former 21-assertion server matrix ended after the first
+  correction and the focused browser check was read-only. It therefore did not
+  exercise remove → exact prior-state restoration → live Bill return → repay.
+  Removal could serialize a blank cell as numeric zero, the Activity client did
+  not refresh Bills state, and replay reused the original immutable marker key.
+  The technical “reopen occurrence” wording also obscured the customer action.
+- Expected result: customers see **Remove payment** or **Remove skip** and the
+  Activity state becomes **Payment removed** or **Skip removed**. Removal
+  restores the exact previous Cash Flow state (blank/formula/value), the Bill
+  returns without a page reload, and a later Pay creates a fresh operation and
+  marker without duplicating the original. Later unrelated entries remain
+  intact.
+- Permanent coverage: the server suite now owns 27 assertions covering exact
+  blank restoration, remove/repay/remove, new operation identity, returned
+  occurrence state, later-entry preservation, Skip, AutoPay, and compensation.
+  The focused browser submits one real removal only in its continuously
+  marker-verified disposable workbook and proves the new wording, confirmation,
+  exact blank state, and live Bill return. Isolated `@259` server run
